#: ../../../css-classes-reference.rst:155
msgid "A note on scopes with sub-scopes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../css-classes-reference.rst:157
msgid ""
"Some scope names above have a ``.`` in them.  We use this notation to "
"specify sub-scopes.  In the generated HTML this will output multiple "
"computed class names. The depth of nesting determines the number of "
"underscores appended to sub-scope names. For example, Lets say the scope is "
"``title.class.other``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../css-classes-reference.rst:162
msgid "The CSS class names generated would be:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../css-classes-reference.rst:164
msgid "``hljs-title``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../css-classes-reference.rst:165
msgid "``class_``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../css-classes-reference.rst:166
msgid "``other__``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../css-classes-reference.rst:168
msgid ""
"The top-level scope is always the one that has the configured prefix applied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../css-classes-reference.rst:170
msgid "The generated HTML would be:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../css-classes-reference.rst:174
msgid "<span class=\"hljs-title class_ other__\">Render</span>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../css-classes-reference.rst:176
msgid "A theme could then simply target that using the following CSS:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../css-classes-reference.rst:178
msgid ""
".hljs-title.class_.other__ {\n"
"   color: blue;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../css-classes-reference.rst:186
msgid "A note on newer scopes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../css-classes-reference.rst:188
msgid ""
"Some scopes have been added more recently and do not enjoy universal theme "
"support.  For themes without support, these items will simply not be "
"highlighted.  This doesn't mean not to use them, only that they will be "
"highlighted better as support improves over time."
msgstr ""

